# Supabase — the SAME project the web app uses, so an account provisioned by
# HR on the web signs straight into this app. Copy this file to `.env`, fill
# both values, restart `expo start`.
#
# Both come from the Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API keys.
#
# These are NOT secrets: the publishable key ships inside every client binary
# by design, and Row Level Security is what protects the data. NEVER put the
# service-role key in this file — it bypasses RLS entirely, and anything
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* is compiled into the app bundle for anyone to read.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ is required: Expo only inlines variables with that prefix into
# the client bundle. Renaming them silently yields `undefined` at runtime.
#
# There is no sign-up and no seed script here. Accounts are provisioned by an
# administrator or HR — from the web console, or via scripts/ in the repo root.

EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_KEY=
